{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>\"Esav her elder son, and Jacob her younger son\"</b> — to emphasize the matter of righteousness, for the custom among parents is to recognize the firstborn in blessing, in honor, and in gifts. And she, knowing the righteousness of the younger and the wickedness of the elder, takes the trouble to do all this to transfer the blessing and the honor from the elder to the younger. And so it says below (Genesis 27:42), \"And the words of Esav her elder son were told to Rebekah, and she sent and called Jacob her younger son.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:35:41.202454895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}